# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators and their structure {#operators-and-their-structure}"
msgstr "Mga operator at ang kanilang istruktura {#operators-and-their-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A bosonic operator is a sum of ordered products of creation and annihilation operators, and a mode can appear more than once in a term. Bosonic operators can also tag their terms with group indices, which later stages use to split a time evolution along physically meaningful pieces. Mappers turn an operator into a qubit operator under a truncation and an encoding. Start here if you are building a Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Ang bosonic operator ay isang sum ng mga naka-order na product ng creation at annihilation operator, at maaaring lumabas nang higit sa isang beses ang isang mode sa isang term. Maaari ring i-tag ng mga bosonic operator ang kanilang mga term gamit ang group index, na ginagamit ng mga susunod na stage para hatiin ang time evolution ayon sa mga pisikal na makabuluhang bahagi. Ginagawang qubit operator ng mga mapper ang isang operator sa ilalim ng truncation at encoding. Magsimula rito kung bumubuo ka ng Hamiltonian.\n"

